<body>

<!-- HEADER -->
<header class="header">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="ticker">NKE · NYSE</div>
    <h1>Nike Inc. Historical Stock Performance Analysis</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A comprehensive 26-year review of price trends, volatility, volume dynamics, and long-term return characteristics from 2000 to 2026.</p>
    <div class="meta">
      <div class="meta-item">Period <span>Jan 3, 2000 – Jan 30, 2026</span></div>
      <div class="meta-item">Trading Days <span>6,559</span></div>
      <div class="meta-item">First Close <span>${first_close:.2f}</span></div>
      <div class="meta-item">Last Close <span>${last_close:.2f}</span></div>
      <div class="meta-item">Report Date <span>April 21, 2026</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- EXECUTIVE SUMMARY -->
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
  <div class="section-label">01 · Executive Summary</div>
  <div class="section-title">Key Performance Indicators</div>
  <div class="section-desc">
    Nike delivered a cumulative return of over 1,200% from January 2000 through January 2026, compounding at approximately 10.6% annually — a strong long-term performance that rewarded patient investors despite multiple severe drawdowns.
  </div>

  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card accent">
      <div class="kpi-label">Cumulative Return</div>
      <div class="kpi-value positive">+{cumret:.0f}%</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">Jan 2000 → Jan 2026</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card green">
      <div class="kpi-label">CAGR</div>
      <div class="kpi-value positive">{cagr:.2f}%</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">Compound annual growth rate</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card red">
      <div class="kpi-label">Maximum Drawdown</div>
      <div class="kpi-value negative">{max_dd:.1f}%</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">Peak: Nov 2021 → Trough: Apr 2025</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card orange">
      <div class="kpi-label">Annualized Volatility</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{ann_vol:.1f}%</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">Based on daily returns ×√252</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card accent">
      <div class="kpi-label">Avg Daily Volume</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{avg_volume/1e6:.1f}M</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">Shares traded per day (mean)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card green">
      <div class="kpi-label">All-Time High</div>
      <div class="kpi-value positive">${ath:.2f}</div>
      <div class="kpi-note">{ath_date}</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- PRICE TREND -->
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
  <div class="section-label">02 · Long-Term Price Trend Analysis</div>
  <div class="section-title">Closing Price History & Market Phases (2000–2026)</div>
  <div class="section-desc">Monthly adjusted closing prices across 26 years. Nike's trajectory spans four distinct structural phases — each shaped by macroeconomic cycles, competitive dynamics, and company-specific catalysts.</div>

  <div class="chart-wrapper">
    <div class="chart-title">NKE Adjusted Closing Price — Monthly (2000–2026)</div>
    <div class="chart-subtitle">Log scale · Adjusted for splits and dividends · Shaded regions indicate major bear markets</div>
    <div class="chart-container" style="height:420px">
      <canvas id="priceChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-wrapper">
    <div class="chart-title">Drawdown from All-Time High (%)</div>
    <div class="chart-subtitle">Percentage decline from the rolling peak closing price at each month-end</div>
    <div class="chart-container" style="height:220px">
      <canvas id="drawdownChart"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3 style="font-size:15px;color:var(--text);margin:28px 0 16px;font-weight:700;">Structural Bull & Bear Phases</h3>
  <table class="phase-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Phase</th>
        <th>Period</th>
        <th>Approx. Return</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>Key Drivers</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Dot-com / Post-Bubble Recovery</td>
        <td>2000 – 2002</td>
        <td style="color:var(--red)">~−45%</td>
        <td><span class="badge badge-bear">Bear</span></td>
        <td>Tech bust, broad equity sell-off, NKE idiosyncratic decline</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Mid-Decade Bull Run</td>
        <td>2003 – 2007</td>
        <td style="color:var(--green)">~+230%</td>
        <td><span class="badge badge-bull">Bull</span></td>
        <td>Global growth, emerging market expansion, brand momentum</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Global Financial Crisis</td>
        <td>2008 – 2009</td>
        <td style="color:var(--red)">~−40%</td>
        <td><span class="badge badge-bear">Bear</span></td>
        <td>Credit crisis, consumer spending collapse, broad risk-off</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Post-Crisis Secular Bull</td>
        <td>2009 – 2021</td>
        <td style="color:var(--green)">~+1,500%</td>
        <td><span class="badge badge-bull">Bull</span></td>
        <td>DTC pivot, China growth, digital acceleration, COVID rebound</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Post-ATH Structural Decline</td>
        <td>2021 – 2025</td>
        <td style="color:var(--red)">~−63%</td>
        <td><span class="badge badge-bear">Bear</span></td>
        <td>Inventory glut, China slowdown, competitive pressure, rate hikes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Partial Stabilization</td>
        <td>2025 – Jan 2026</td>
        <td style="color:var(--orange)">~−12%</td>
        <td><span class="badge badge-mixed">Mixed</span></td>
        <td>New CEO, restructuring, macro uncertainty</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
</section>

<!-- VOLATILITY -->
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
  <div class="section-label">03 · Volatility & Risk Assessment</div>
  <div class="section-title">Rolling Volatility & Daily Price Ranges</div>
  <div class="section-desc">Annualized volatility (252-day rolling window) measures realized risk over time. Spikes correspond to crisis episodes; structurally elevated volatility in 2024–2025 reflects the post-peak deterioration.</div>

  <div class="chart-wrapper">
