<!-- KEY TAKEAWAYS -->
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
  <div class="section-label">06 · Key Takeaways & Investment Implications</div>
  <div class="section-title">Synthesis for Long-Term Investors</div>
  <div class="section-desc">Grounded in the 26-year data record, these observations reflect NKE's empirical risk-return profile as a large-cap consumer discretionary compounder.</div>

  <ul class="takeaway-list">
    <li data-num="1"><strong>Exceptional long-term compounder, with painful entry-point sensitivity.</strong> A $10,000 investment at the start of 2000 grew to approximately $138,000 by January 2026 (+1,282%). However, an investor entering at the November 2021 ATH of $166.25 would have lost over 60% by April 2025, illustrating that even outstanding businesses carry severe timing risk.</li>
    <li data-num="2"><strong>The 2010s were the golden decade.</strong> NKE compounded at an estimated 22% CAGR across the decade — driven by DTC transformation, China expansion, and a low-rate environment. This decade alone accounts for the majority of lifetime total return. Replication requires similar structural tailwinds.</li>
    <li data-num="3"><strong>Maximum drawdown of −68.5% demands robust position sizing.</strong> Three distinct drawdowns exceeded −40% (2000–2002, 2008–2009, 2021–2025). Investors applying standard portfolio construction (e.g., 5–10% single-stock allocation) would have experienced severe paper losses that tested conviction — and many capitulated near troughs.</li>
    <li data-num="4"><strong>Volume spikes are a reliable signal of regime change.</strong> The highest-volume days (Jun 2024: 130M shares, Jun 2025: 117M shares) all occurred during sharp downside moves. Elevated volume during declining prices — the "distribution" signature — preceded extended bear phases in every major cycle observed.</li>
    <li data-num="5"><strong>31.2% annualized volatility classifies NKE as a high-volatility large-cap.</strong> At 31.2% vol, NKE exceeded what many investors expect from blue-chip consumer names. Risk-adjusted return (Sharpe proxy) was positive but modest, suggesting the compounding was earned through tolerance of significant variance — not smooth appreciation.</li>
    <li data-num="6"><strong>The 2020s mark a structural reset, not yet a recovery.</strong> As of January 2026, NKE trades at $61.81 — a level last seen in mid-2017, erasing seven years of price appreciation. Whether this represents a mean-reversion opportunity or a new lower-growth regime depends on competitive dynamics, China recovery, and strategic execution under new leadership.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
</section>

